[{"headline":"Why Are Social Leaders Dying in Colombia’s Cauca?","author_name":["Maria Alejandra Navarrete","Chris Dalby"],"publication_date":"2019-10-16T00:00:00.000Z","article_body":"\n\n\t\t\n\t\t<div id=\"page-position-marker_id_341335\" class=\"page-position-marker\" style=\"position: absolute; top: 50%\"></div><div id=\"page-position-marker_id_345179\" class=\"page-position-marker\" style=\"position: absolute; top: 15%\"></div><div id=\"page-position-marker_id_348919\" class=\"page-position-marker\" style=\"position: absolute; top: 30%\"></div>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In early 2018, Colombia’s </span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Ombudsman’s Office sounded the alarm regarding an unprecedented increase in the murders of social leaders nationwide. Over 18 months later, the situation has only gotten worse, with the southwestern department of Cauca bearing the brunt of these killings.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In February 2018, the Ombudsman’s Office <a href=\"http://www.indepaz.org.co/wp-content/uploads/2018/03/AT-N%C2%B0-026-18-Defensores.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">published&nbsp;</a></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">an initial alert, reporting 697 cases of violence against human rights activists and leaders of social organizations between 2016 and 2018.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">In a 2019 <a href=\"https://insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Informe-seguimiento-AT-026-18_agosto-2019-1.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">follow-up report</a>, the entity documented 1,335 cases of leaders affected by threats, attacks and homicides, representing a more than 90 percent increase in just one year.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"color: #800000;\"><b>SEE ALSO: </b></span><a href=\"https://insightcrime.org/colombia-organized-crime-news/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Colombia News and Profile</span></a></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">These acts of aggression have been focused on local community leaders, rural farmers and indigenous representatives who work to defend their territories.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Antioquia, Norte de Santander and Cauca have <a href=\"https://www.telesurtv.net/news/continua-genocidio-lideres-sociales-colombia-20190602-0012.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">historically accounted</a> for most such attacks, but&nbsp;</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">the number of individuals affected in Cauca has </span><a href=\"https://www.eltiempo.com/colombia/otras-ciudades/el-mapa-de-los-lideres-sociales-asesinados-en-colombia-184408\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">dramatically increased</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;in the last two years. The United Nations (UN) has reported 36 killings of indigenous leaders alone in Cauca in 2019, alongside eight more attempted murders and 53 death threats, <a href=\"https://www.telesurtv.net/news/colombia-asesinato-guardia-indigena-toribio-canas-cauca-20191014-0023.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">reported</a> TeleSUR.</span></p>\n<aside>\t\t\t<div class=\"newspack-popup-container newspack-popup hidden   newspack-inline-popup       \" role=\"button\" tabindex=\"0\" style=\"background-color:#FFFFFF;color:#000\" id=\"id_345170\" data-segments=\"4675\" data-frequency=\"0,0,1,day\">\n\t\t\t\t\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover class-en\" style=\"min-height:329px;aspect-ratio:unset;\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"780\" height=\"407\" class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-345176 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=780%2C407&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1\" style=\"object-position:12% 82%\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" data-object-position=\"12% 82%\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?w=1737&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 1737w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=300%2C156&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=1024%2C534&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=768%2C401&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=1536%2C801&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=1200%2C626&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=780%2C407&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 780w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=400%2C209&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 400w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=706%2C368&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 706w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?w=370&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 370w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 780px) 100vw, 780px\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-dark-gray-background-color has-background-dim-90 has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-block-cover-is-layout-constrained\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-left has-secondary-color has-text-color has-link-color has-large-font-size wp-elements-1\" id=\"h-you-trust-our-reporting-we-need-your-support\" style=\"padding-top:0;padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80);padding-bottom:0;padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80);font-style:normal;font-weight:400;text-transform:none\"><em>You Trust our Reporting, <mark style=\"background-color:#201f2c;color:#ebbb0c\" class=\"has-inline-color\">We Need Your Support.</mark></em></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-secondary-color has-text-color has-link-color wp-elements-2 wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"padding-top:0;padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80)\">With a regular donation from $50, or a single donation from $15, you can have access to exclusive benefits. Your support is crucial for us to keep doing what we do.</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\" style=\"padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80)\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button has-custom-width wp-block-button__width-50 is-style-fill\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-dark-gray-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color has-normal-font-size has-custom-font-size wp-element-button\" href=\"https://insightcrime.org/donate/?utm_source=web&amp;utm_medium=banner&amp;utm_campaign=Donation_campaign\" style=\"background-color:#ebbb0c;padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)\">Donate Now</a></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button has-custom-width wp-block-button__width-50 is-style-outline is-style-outline--3\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-secondary-variation-color has-text-color has-link-color has-normal-font-size has-custom-font-size wp-element-button\" href=\"https://insightcrime.org/donate/?utm_source=web&amp;utm_medium=banner&amp;utm_campaign=Donation_campaign#already-donor-block\" style=\"padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)\"><strong>I’m already a donor</strong></a></div>\n</div>\n</div></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-cover class-es\" style=\"min-height:329px;aspect-ratio:unset;\"><img data-recalc-dims=\"1\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"780\" height=\"407\" class=\"wp-block-cover__image-background wp-image-345176 size-large\" alt=\"\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=780%2C407&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1\" style=\"object-position:12% 82%\" data-object-fit=\"cover\" data-object-position=\"12% 82%\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?w=1737&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 1737w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=300%2C156&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 300w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=1024%2C534&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 1024w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=768%2C401&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=1536%2C801&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 1536w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=1200%2C626&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=780%2C407&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 780w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=400%2C209&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 400w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?resize=706%2C368&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 706w, https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/06/Cover-InSight-Crime.png?w=370&amp;quality=100&amp;ssl=1 370w\" sizes=\"(max-width: 780px) 100vw, 780px\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"wp-block-cover__background has-dark-gray-background-color has-background-dim-90 has-background-dim\"></span><div class=\"wp-block-cover__inner-container is-layout-constrained wp-block-cover-is-layout-constrained\">\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading has-text-align-left has-secondary-color has-text-color has-link-color has-large-font-size wp-elements-3\" id=\"h-usted-confia-en-nuestro-periodismo-nosotros-confiamos-en-su-apoyo\" style=\"padding-top:0;padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80);padding-bottom:0;padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80);font-style:normal;font-weight:400;text-transform:none\"><em>Usted confia en nuestro periodismo, <mark style=\"background-color:#201f2c;color:#ebbb0c\" class=\"has-inline-color\">nosotros confiamos en su apoyo.</mark></em></h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"has-secondary-color has-text-color has-link-color wp-elements-4 wp-block-paragraph\" style=\"padding-top:0;padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80);padding-bottom:var(--wp--preset--spacing--30);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80)\">Con una donación recurrente desde US$50 o una donación única desde US$15, podrá acceder a beneficios exclusivos. Su apoyo es fundamental para seguir investigando y analizando el crimen organizado en América Latina y el Caribe.</p>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-buttons is-layout-flex wp-block-buttons-is-layout-flex\" style=\"padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--80)\">\n<div class=\"wp-block-button has-custom-width wp-block-button__width-50 is-style-fill\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-dark-gray-color has-text-color has-background has-link-color has-normal-font-size has-custom-font-size wp-element-button\" href=\"https://insightcrime.org/es/donar/?utm_source=web&amp;utm_medium=banner&amp;utm_campaign=Donation_campaign\" style=\"background-color:#ebbb0c;padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)\">Donar ahora</a></div>\n\n\n\n<div class=\"wp-block-button has-custom-width wp-block-button__width-50 is-style-outline is-style-outline--4\"><a class=\"wp-block-button__link has-secondary-variation-color has-text-color has-link-color has-normal-font-size has-custom-font-size wp-element-button\" href=\"https://insightcrime.org/es/donar/?utm_source=web&amp;utm_medium=banner&amp;utm_campaign=Donation_campaign#ya-donante-bloque\" style=\"padding-right:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60);padding-left:var(--wp--preset--spacing--60)\"><strong>Ya so</strong>y donante</a></div>\n</div>\n</div></div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t</aside>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">According to an <a href=\"https://insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/Informe-seguimiento-AT-026-18_agosto-2019-1.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ombudsman’s Office report</a>, the municipalities most blighted by this violence are Miranda, Corinto and Caloto, all key transit points for drug shipments destined to leave the country via the Pacific Ocean.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The latest killing <a href=\"https://www.eluniversal.com.co/colombia/indigenas-del-suroeste-de-colombia-denuncian-el-asesinato-de-otro-lider-HM1871955\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">happened</a> on October 13 when&nbsp;Toribio Canas, an indigenous leader in the municipality of&nbsp;Toribío, was shot dead. Starting in 2000, Canas had reportedly been in charge of organizing an “indigenous guard” in the area to reclaim land.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">According to <a href=\"https://www.elespectador.com/noticias/nacional/cauca/asesinan-toribio-canas-guardia-indigena-del-norte-del-cauca-articulo-886040\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">El Espectador</a>, the UN Office of the High Commissioner for Human Rights has counted at least nine indigenous leaders killed in Cauca since September.</p>\n\n<h3 class=\"wp-block-heading\">InSight Crime Analysis</h3>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">While Cauca has seen the worst of the violence against local community leaders in 2019, the motives for these killings reflect the wider reasons for such targeted violence across Colombia.&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">According to the organization</span><a href=\"https://somosdefensores.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/Informe-comunales_final.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Somos Defensores</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, one of the main reasons social leaders are targeted is due to their participation in the implementation of the 2016 peace agreement with the Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia (Fuerzas Armadas Revolucionarias de Colombia –&nbsp;FARC).</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Social leaders can also run afoul of criminal groups when trying to stem the tide of illegal economies within their communities. Many victims were involved in activities related to <a href=\"https://insightcrime.org/news/analysis/a-death-foretold-colombias-crop-substitution-program/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">coca crop substitution</a>, the creation of legal jobs, or <a href=\"https://globalriskinsights.com/2017/10/land-farc-future-colombia/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">land redistribution</a>, all efforts which can curtail drug production and help rural residents find sustainable alternatives.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"color: #800000;\"><b>SEE ALSO: </b></span><a href=\"https://insightcrime.org/news/analysis/why-political-candidates-assassinated-colombia/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Why Are Political Candidates Being Assassinated in Colombia?</span></a></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">According to the Institute for Development and Peace Studies</span><a href=\"http://www.indepaz.org.co/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/Informe-Violaciones-a-los-Derechos-Humanos-en-tiempos-de-Paz.-Septiembre-de-2019-18-09-19.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> (</span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Instituto de Estudios para el Desarrollo y la Paz – INDEPAZ)</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">, other risk factors contributing to violence against social leaders include denunciations of armed actors, accusations of mismanagement of public funds by State entities, and claims to the right to use natural resources.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">As </span><a href=\"https://moe.org.co/wp-content/uploads/2019/09/20190827-_Informe_ViolPol.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">reported</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> by Colombia’s Electoral Observation Mission (Misión de Observación Electoral – MOE), many of these risk factors escalate during election season. By mid-September, seven politicians <a href=\"https://insightcrime.org/news/analysis/why-political-candidates-assassinated-colombia/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">had been killed</a> ahead of upcoming local elections in late October.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The problems facing social leaders in Cauca are exacerbated by the department’s crucial location as a drug trafficking corridor.&nbsp;</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">According to the latest </span><a href=\"https://www.unodc.org/documents/colombia/2019/Agosto/Informe_de_Monitoreo_de_Territorios_Afectador_por_Cultivos_Ilicitos_en_Colombia_2018_.pdf\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">report</span></a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\"> by the United Nations Office on Drugs and Crime (UNODC), around 17,000 hectares of coca were produced in this department alone in 2018.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cauca’s location along the Naya River corridor, which connects the country’s central mountain range to the coasts of the Pacific Ocean through kilometers of thick jungle, makes it a necessary transit point for drug shipments.</span></p>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Cauca has therefore become <a href=\"https://www.semana.com/nacion/articulo/disputas-entre-bandas-criminales-aumentan-la-violencia-en-valle-y-cauca/622289\">hotly contested</a> by a range of criminal groups, seeking an advantage there, including the National Liberation Army (Ejército de Liberación Nacional – ELN), the Popular Liberation Army (Ejército Popular de Liberación – EPL) and at least five dissident fronts of the Revolutionary Armed Forces of Colombia (Fuerzas Armadas Revolucionarias de Colombia – FARC) are reported as having a presence in this department. </span></p>\n\t","article_url":"https://insightcrime.org/news/analysis-murders-social-leaders-cauca-colombia/","country_region":"Colombia, Cauca","categories":["News"],"featured_image":"https://i0.wp.com/insightcrime.org/wp-content/uploads/2019/10/5b58fe66132a0.jpeg?fit=350%2C250&quality=100&ssl=1","input":{"url":"https://insightcrime.org/news/analysis/"}}]